LU: DP_ Longest Common Subsequence 3 Strings
Success rate: 54.55%

Given three strings A, B, and C, find the length of the longest subsequence that is common to all three strings.

Input Format:
A: The first string.
B: The second string.
C: The third string.

Output Format:
The length of the longest common subsequence present in all three strings.

Constraints:
1 <= n1, n2, n3 <= 20

Sample test cases
Input
aab
abc
abac
Expected output

2

